---
/** DRAFT: the home page's introduction, under the hero. */
---

<section class="intro" aria-labelledby="intro-h">
  <div class="wrap grid">
    <div>
      <h2 id="intro-h">What DynShift builds</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="body">
      <p class="big">
        Software that does one job properly: products you install and use, and
        tools for the people who build software.
      </p>
      <p>
        The first product is <a href="/projects/phonepad/">PhonePad</a>, which turns
        an Android phone into a wireless Xbox-compatible controller for a Windows
        PC, with nothing to buy and nothing sent anywhere but your own computer.
        The tools are <a href="/projects/layr/">LAYR</a>, a compiled language for
        web layout written in a design's own numbers, and a set of small
        <a href="/packages/">Flutter packages</a> on pub.dev.
      </p>
      <p>
        Each project is built one at a time, released when it does the whole job
        it set out to do, and documented with the measurements and the source
        needed to check it. Almost all of it is open source: GPL-3.0 for products,
        MIT for libraries.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .intro {
    padding-block: clamp(48px, 8vw, 104px) clamp(32px, 5vw, 56px);
  }
  .grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 2fr);
    gap: 20px clamp(32px, 6vw, 96px);
    align-items: start;
  }
  .big {
    font-size: clamp(1.35rem, 2.4vw, 1.75rem);
    line-height: 1.35;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 500;
    max-width: 30ch;
    text-wrap: balance;
    margin-bottom: 0.9em;
  }
  .body p:not(.big) {
    color: var(--ink2);
    font-size: 1.04rem;
    max-width: 58ch;
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }
  @media (max-width: 820px) {
    .grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
